----- stdout -----
Check files against the policies

Usage: zoll check [OPTIONS] [PATHS]...

Arguments:
  [PATHS]...  Files and directories to check [default: .]

Options:
      --config <PATH>      This config instead of the one found from the working directory up
      --format <FORMAT>    How violations are printed [default: text] [possible values: text, json, github, sarif]
      --color <WHEN>       When to color the output [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --fail-on <FAIL_ON>  Which results fail the run; overrides the config's `fail-on` [possible values: deny, warn]
      --locked             Fail when `zoll.lock` does not match the config's git policies
      --show-files         List the files that would be checked, each with its language, and check none
      --force-exclude      Leave out a file named in PATHS that `exclude` leaves out, as a pre-commit hook needs: it names every staged file
  -h, --help               Print help

